From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Keep UCSI registration and connector ownership accurate

Do not record a failed synchronous ucsi_register() as a live registration.
Leave later service events able to register the interface, and avoid issuing
unregister for an interface whose version read never succeeded.

Clear the connector pointer after releasing it. PMIC GLINK reuses the UCSI
instance across firmware service restarts; if the next initialization fails
before allocating connectors, another unregister must not use the old array.

Adapted from yzddmr6's registration fix and Codex's connector cleanup fix:
https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/9f9cd5ac3bc1fade2c2584a051913a2b03d506d2
https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/f43a4aa7fa89c6e227c5ec763e695576e66e2eb7
The existing work cancellation and port teardown ordering are retained.

--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
@@ -316,13 +316,18 @@ static void pmic_glink_ucsi_register(struct work_struct *work)
 	struct pmic_glink_ucsi *ucsi = container_of(work, struct pmic_glink_ucsi, register_work);
 	unsigned long flags;
 	bool pd_running;
+	int ret;
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&ucsi->state_lock, flags);
 	pd_running = ucsi->pd_running;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ucsi->state_lock, flags);
 
 	if (!ucsi->ucsi_registered && pd_running) {
-		ucsi_register(ucsi->ucsi);
+		ret = ucsi_register(ucsi->ucsi);
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(ucsi->dev, "UCSI registration failed: %d\n", ret);
+			return;
+		}
 		ucsi->ucsi_registered = true;
 	} else if (ucsi->ucsi_registered && !pd_running) {
 		ucsi_unregister(ucsi->ucsi);
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -2493,6 +2493,7 @@ void ucsi_unregister(struct ucsi *ucsi)
 	}
 
 	kfree(ucsi->connector);
+	ucsi->connector = NULL;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ucsi_unregister);
 
